":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.95609,"donor_log2fc":-0.0606027,"donor_lfcse":0.204568,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00302265},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"SNAPIN","gene_symbol_current":"SNAPIN","gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.00169285,"nucleus_log2fc":0.318429,"nucleus_score":3.64562,"pct_ad":0.125857,"pct_control":0.105334,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.254106,"donor_lfcse":0.185127,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":7.736e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"SNAPIN","gene_symbol_current":"SNAPIN","gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.919976,"donor_log2fc":0.101318,"donor_lfcse":0.156177,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0043559}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","module":"turquoise","kme":0.163515,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","module":"turquoise","kme":0.196054,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.524491,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","module":"turquoise","kme":0.134948,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","module":"turquoise","kme":0.14623,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000143553","entrez_id":["23557"],"uniprot":["O95295"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a coiled-coil-forming protein that associates with the SNARE (soluble N-ethylmaleimide-sensitive fusion protein attachment protein receptor) complex of proteins and the BLOC-1 (biogenesis of lysosome-related organelles) complex. Biochemical studies have identified additional binding partners. As part of the SNARE complex, it is required for vesicle docking and fusion and regulates neurotransmitter release. The BLOC-1 complex is required for the biogenesis of specialized organelles such as melanosomes and platelet dense granules. Mutations in gene products that form the BLOC-1 complex have been identified in mouse strains that are models of Hermansky-Pudlak syndrome. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Jun 2012].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O95295","text":"Component of the BLOC-1 complex, a complex that is required for normal biogenesis of lysosome-related organelles (LRO), such as platelet dense granules and melanosomes. In concert with the AP-3 complex, the BLOC-1 complex is required to target membrane protein cargos into vesicles assembled at cell bodies for delivery into neurites and nerve terminals. The BLOC-1 complex, in association with SNARE proteins, is also proposed to be involved in neurite extension. Plays a role in intracellular vesicle trafficking and synaptic vesicle recycling. May modulate a step between vesicle priming, fusion and calcium-dependent neurotransmitter release through its ability to potentiate the interaction of synaptotagmin with the SNAREs and the plasma-membrane-associated protein SNAP25. Its phosphorylation state influences exocytotic protein interactions and may regulate synaptic vesicle exocytosis. May also have a role in the mechanisms of SNARE-mediated membrane fusion in non-neuronal cells (PubMed:17182842, PubMed:18167355). As part of the BORC complex may play a role in lysosomes movement and localization at the cell periphery. Associated with the cytosolic face of lysosomes, the BORC complex may recruit ARL8B and couple lysosomes to microtubule plus-end-directed kinesin motor (PubMed:25898167)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}